# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values (or just run ./install.sh,
# which does all of this interactively and is safe to re-run any time).
# cp .env.example .env

# ── Which services actually start ───────────────────────────────────────────
# See "Deployment modes" in README.md. A service not listed in any active
# profile below is never started — this isn't optional, pick one:
#   station-core,station-ui        Local station (full stack + local dashboard)
#   cloud,license                  Cloud server only (no station hardware)
#   station-core                   Poll-sync station (no local dashboard)
#   station-core,station-ui,cloud,license  Complete / demo (everything, one box)
COMPOSE_PROFILES=station-core,station-ui

# Database password (used by db, api, and poller services)
DB_PASSWORD=tls_local

# Secret key for API session tokens (generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))")
SECRET_KEY=change-me-in-production

# Optional: override serial port if different from config/tls-decoded.yaml
# SERIAL_PORT=/dev/ttyUSB0

# Optional: override host-side ports if the defaults collide with something
# else already running on this box (common on a shared/home server) —
# these only change the HOST side of the mapping, containers still talk to
# each other on their normal internal ports regardless.
# DB_PORT=5432
# API_PORT=8000
# FRONTEND_PORT=5005

# ── Commander price sync (optional — poller + api, station side) ──────────────
# Wires hourly fuel prices from a commander-reader instance (read-only REST
# proxy in front of a Verifone Commander) into this station's pricing. Leave
# COMMANDER_READER_URL blank/unset to skip this entirely — the poller just
# no-ops. Per-tank grade id mapping is set in the dashboard's Settings ->
# tank editor, not here (grade ids aren't portable across stations).
# COMMANDER_READER_URL=http://<commander-reader-host>:8200
# COMMANDER_PRICE_TIER=cash          # or "credit"
# COMMANDER_PRICE_SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60
# COMMANDER_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MINUTES=5   # cheap /health-only check, keeps
                                            # Settings -> Commander price sync
                                            # showing current status

# Note: enabled/URL/tier/interval above are also editable live from
# Settings -> Commander price sync once the app is running — these env vars
# only matter for the very first boot.

# Applied to new price entries when a tax rate isn't given explicitly, so
# it's configured once here instead of re-entered on every price change.
# Used by both api (manual entries) and poller (Commander-synced entries).
# Also editable live from Settings -> Tax rate afterward.
# DEFAULT_TAX_RATE_PERCENT=9.75

# ── Cloud sync (optional — sync service, station side) ────────────────────────
# Only needed if this station should push to a cloud hub. Leave blank/unset
# to keep this station fully local-only — sync just idles. Can also be set
# later, live, from the local dashboard's Settings -> Cloud sync panel
# instead of here — see cloud/README.md.
# CLOUD_INGEST_URL=http://<cloud-host>:8100
# STATION_DEVICE_ID=
# STATION_DEVICE_SECRET=
# SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES=30

# ── Cloud hub (optional — cloud-db/cloud-api/cloud-frontend services) ─────────
# Only needed if this box is also running the cloud hub section of
# docker-compose.yml (or you commented that section out). See cloud/README.md.
# CLOUD_DB_PASSWORD=change-me
# CLOUD_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# CLOUD_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
# CLOUD_DB_PORT=5433
# CLOUD_API_PORT=8100
# CLOUD_FRONTEND_PORT=5100

# ── License server (optional — profile "license") ─────────────────────────────
# Only needed alongside "cloud" — see license-server/README.md. A simple
# database of hand-issued, use-limited passphrases — no signing keys, no
# license files. LICENSE_SERVER_ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH gates every /admin/* route
# (list/create/renew/suspend licenses); it's a HASH, not the token itself —
# run `python3 license-server/hash_secret.py` to generate it, the plaintext
# never goes in this file. Leaving it unset makes the service refuse all
# admin routes (fails loud, not open) — set your own before issuing real
# licenses. MASTER_PASSPHRASE optionally overrides the auto-seeded
# unlimited-use, never-expiring master code (default "PermissionGranted200").
# LICENSE_SERVER_ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH=
# MASTER_PASSPHRASE=
# LICENSE_SERVER_PORT=8200

# ── Cloud Utility licensing (optional — cloud-api only) ────────────────────────
# The Cloud Utility itself checks a license; the Local Instance never does
# (see license-server/README.md). One passphrase, always phoned home to the
# license server — no offline verification.
#
# CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY below is an INITIAL-DEPLOYMENT CONVENIENCE ONLY — it
# seeds the license exactly once, the very first time this container starts
# against an empty database. After that, activating or switching to a new
# passphrase is done from Admin -> License in the cloud frontend (no
# restart) — this env var is never read again once a license has been
# configured either way. Leave it blank to skip the seed and configure
# entirely from the UI on first login instead.
#
# --- Deployment/infra settings — these DO always come from env, never the UI ---
# LICENSE_SERVER_URL=http://license-server:8000
# LICENSE_CHECK_INTERVAL_HOURS=24
# LICENSE_GRACE_DAYS=45
#
# --- Seed (first boot only, see above) ---
# CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY=                     # a passphrase issued via license-server's POST /admin/licenses
